; Synthesis #817: Cutout x RLCT - L3 MeTTa Encoding\n; Date: 2026-10-29\n; Status: L3\n; Pipeline: L0 done L1 done L2 done L3 done L4 PENDING\n\n; ---- Type Declarations ----\n(: Parameter Type)\n(: Input Type)\n(: Mask Type)\n(: MaskSize Type)\n(: Loss Type)\n(: Fiber Type)\n(: RLCT Type)\n(: Epsilon Type)\n(: ProbabilityDist Type)\n(: Stratum Type)\n\n; ---- D1: Input Space and Square Mask ----\n(= (input_space X R^d) )\n(= (square_mask M (fn h0 w0 l)\n   (indicator (and (>= i (- h0 (/ l 2))) (<= i (+ h0 (/ l 2)))\n                   (>= j (- w0 (/ l 2))) (<= j (+ w0 (/ l 2)))))))\n\n; ---- D2: Cutout Masked Input ----\n(= (cutout_input (fn x M) (* x M)))\n\n; ---- D3: Cutout Loss ----\n(= (cutout_loss_single (fn theta x y M)\n   (ce (f (cutout_input x M) theta) y)))\n(= (cutout_loss (fn theta)\n   (/ (sum_n (E_M (cutout_loss_single theta x_n y_n M_n))) N)))\n\n; ---- D4: Piecewise Structure ----\n(= (grad_cutout (fn theta M)\n   (gradient theta (cutout_loss_single theta x y M))))\n\n; ---- D5: Cutout as Stochastic Loss Family ----\n(= (cutout_expected (fn theta l)\n   (integral h0 w0 (cutout_loss_single theta x y (square_mask h0 w0 l))\n             (* (- H l) (- W l)))))\n\n; ---- D6: Singular Fiber Structure ----\n(= (V_M (fn M)\n   (set theta (correct (f (cutout_input x M) theta) y))))\n(= (V_cutout (fn l)\n   (intersect_M (V_M (square_mask h0 w0 l)))))\n\n; ---- D7: RLCT Definition ----\n(= (L_star (fn) (min_theta (cutout_loss theta))))\n(= (lambda_cutout (fn l)\n   (lim eps 0 (/ (log (* (inv (N eps)) (integral (exp (* -beta (- (cutout_loss theta) (L_star)))) dtheta))) (log (inv eps)))))\n\n; ---- C1 (PROVEN): R_an,exp Definability ----\n(|- ((==> (R_an_exp_definable (square_mask M)) (stv 1.0 0.95))\n    ((R_an_exp_definable (ce (f x theta) y)) (stv 1.0 0.95))\n    ((R_an_exp_definable (cutout_loss theta)) (stv 1.0 0.95)))\n\n; ---- C2 (CONJECTURAL): Cutout Singular Fiber as Mask Intersection ----\n(|~ ((Implication (Inheritance V_cutout (IntSet MaskIntersectionFiber))\n     (Subset V_cutout V_0)) (stv 0.6 0.7))\n(|~ ((Implication (Inheritance V_cutout (IntSet MaskIntersectionFiber))\n     (GreaterOrEqual (codim V_cutout) (codim V_0))) (stv 0.55 0.7))\n\n; ---- C3 (CONJECTURAL): Mask Size L as Stratum Selector ----\n(|~ ((Implication (Equal l 0)\n     (Equal (V_cutout l) V_0)) (stv 0.7 0.8))\n(|~ ((Implication (GreaterOrEqual l H)\n     (Equal (V_cutout l) EmptySet)) (stv 0.7 0.8))\n(|~ ((Implication (LessThan l L_star)\n     (NonEmpty (V_cutout l))) (stv 0.5 0.7))\n(|~ ((Implication (GreaterThan l L_star)\n     (Empty (V_cutout l))) (stv 0.5 0.7))\n\n; ---- C4 (CONJECTURAL): Generalization Bound ----\n(|~ ((Implication (And (Inheritance theta V_cutout) (Transversality V_M1 V_M2))\n     (Equal (lambda_cutout l) (+ (lambda_0) (sum_M (delta_M)))) (stv 0.5 0.7))\n(|~ ((Implication (NonTransverse (intersect_M (V_M M)))\n     (LessThan (lambda_cutout l) (+ (lambda_0) (sum_M (delta_M)))) (stv 0.5 0.65))\n\n; ---- C5 (CONJECTURAL): Spatial Contiguity Singularity ----\n(|~ ((Implication (And (Inheritance M_contig Mask) (Inheritance M_indep Mask))\n     (LessThan (lambda_cutout_contig) (lambda_cutout_indep))) (stv 0.55 0.7))\n\n; ---- Caveats ----\n; C1: Square mask is semialgebraic (4 polynomial inequalities). Softmax is exp-definable. Finite sum closure. Integration over semialgebraic domain is definable. QED.\n; C2: Intersection of infinitely many V_M may create singularities even if individual V_M are smooth. Non-transverse intersections expected. Codim increases with independent mask constraints.\n; C3: L=0 gives V_0 (identity mask). L>=H gives empty set. L* conjectured related to effective receptive field size. SGLD prediction: LLC kink at L*. Monotonicity of lambda in L is conjectural.\n; C4: Additive lambda under transversality. Non-transverse intersections yield lower-dimensional strata with lower RLCT. Effective sample size increase heuristic.\n; C5: Contiguous masking preserves spatial correlation. Independent pixel masking destroys it. Conjecture: lambda_contig < lambda_indep for same mask ratio. Edge effects tied to receptive field geometry.\n\n; ---- Cross-References ----\n; #8 (RLCT definability), #16 (semialgebraic sets), #169 (Dropout x RLCT), #532 (CutMix x RLCT)\n; #590 (Adversarial Training x RLCT), #615 (Consistency Regularization x RLCT)\n; #816 (VAT x RLCT), #97 (SGD), #100 (gradient descent)